ASSESSMENT

Primary Diagnosis: Undiagnosed Coeliac Disease - Status: Decompensated malabsorption state
Differentials:

Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) - Ruled out/unlikely due to: The presence of profound "red flag" symptoms including refractory iron deficiency anemia, severe steatorrhea, and unintentional weight loss, which completely exclude a functional benign bowel disorder.

Crohn's Disease - Ruled out/unlikely due to: Absence of gross bloody diarrhea, perianal fistulizing disease, or severe right lower quadrant inflammatory masses, though endoscopic evaluation is required to definitively differentiate.

Chronic Pancreatitis - Ruled out/unlikely due to: Absence of a history of severe acute pancreatic pain episodes, lack of significant alcohol history, and the presence of concurrent autoimmune-appearing skin rashes (dermatitis herpetiformis).
